{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ובא אליה", :translit "u-va eleha", :gloss "and he comes to her"} {:he "ובא אליה מלך גדול", :translit "u-va eleha melekh gadol", :gloss "and he came to her, a great king"} {:he "יצה\"ר", :translit "yetzer ha-ra", :gloss "evil inclination"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ובא אליה" "ובא אליה מלך גדול"]} {:kind :other, :note "Derash links the phrase to the evil inclination; moralizing application to the verse's context."}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'ובא אליה מלך גדול' occurs in 1 Kings 14:21, describing Rehoboam's mother Naamah the Ammonitess. The rabbis expound visits to forbidden relations as driven by the yetzer ha-ra, as in Sukkah 52b where the yetzer ha-ra is described as overpowering. The scene in Deuteronomy 22:13-14, where a husband develops hatred toward his wife and publicly defames her, is read midrashically as the consequence of yielding to the evil inclination, consistent with the warning of Proverbs 5:3-4 about the bitter end of following desire.", :sources ["1 Kings 14:21" "Sukkah 52b" "Proverbs 5:3-4"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ובא אליה" "ובא אליה מלך גדול"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ובא אליה", :refs ["Deuteronomy 22:13" "Ecclesiastes 9:14"], :n 2, :lens :exact} {:phrase "ובא אליה מלך גדול", :refs ["Ecclesiastes 9:14"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :other, :note "Derash links the phrase to the evil inclination; moralizing application to the verse's context.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:38:23.293261720Z", :model "glm-5.2"}